>>__ load "simpExtLib";
>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `add_unsafe_solver`

``` hol4
simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver : TraverseExt.ssolver ->
  simpExtLib.simpset -> simpExtLib.simpset
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Adds an unsafe solver to an extension simpset.

Solvers have the types

``` hol4
type TraverseExt.ssolver =
  {name : string, solve : simp_prover_ctxt -> term -> thm}
type TraverseExt.simp_prover_ctxt =
  {stack : term list, context_thms : thm list, recurse : term -> thm}
```

`solve ctxt c` must prove `c` or raise `HOL_ERR`. In `ctxt`, `stack` holds
the side conditions already being attempted, `context_thms` the theorems
in the simplifier's context (supplied theorems, assumptions and facts
assumed by congruence rules), and `recurse c` simplifies `c`, returning
`|- c = c'`.

Unsafe solvers prove the side conditions of conditional rewrites that
the subgoaler (see `simpExtLib.set_subgoaler`) does not reduce to `T`;
they are tried on the subgoaler's result. They are also the final solvers of
`simpExtLib.GEN_SIMP_TAC {safe = false}`. The solver is added after the
existing unsafe solvers, unless one with the same name is already present,
in which case the simpset is unchanged.

### Failure

Never fails.

### Example

``` hol4
>>_ val decide : TraverseExt.ssolver = {name = "decide", solve = K DECIDE};
>> simpExtLib.SIMP_CONV
     (simpExtLib.add_unsafe_solver decide
        (simpExtLib.lift_simpset boolSimps.bool_ss))
     [arithmeticTheory.LESS_MOD] “x MOD (x + 1)”;
```

